WEBVTT

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.230
The O'bli are advancing into the real world.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.990
The only case we have of the 
O'bli crossing dimensions

00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:10.480
is the incident on the snowy mountain, moshu.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.360
If the O'bli appear in a town and 
start attacking just anyone...

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:18.580
It'll be impossible to resolve everything 
with the Fifth Force alone.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.310
Tsubame-san?

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.630
It's nothing.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.080
<i>It couldn't be...</i>

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:05.180
<b>Change! The Three Sisters Have Disappeared</b>

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:21.280
The three Origami sisters 
haven't come to school?

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:23.810
They've been absent for three days already.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.910
Niho-chin, you guys saw them last 
on the snowy mountain, right?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.970
Do you know something?

00:02:29.970 --> 00:02:32.780
Nothing particularly strange happened...

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:35.170
Maybe they're just busy with their jobs?

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.420
Maybe...

00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:41.970
I could have introduced them to a job 
if they were in that much trouble.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.560
It's worrisome that the three of 
them haven't come to school.

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:47.740
Yeah.

00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:51.430
Maybe they're just working, 
like Niho-san says.

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.940
Or one of them got sick, 
and they're all taking care of her?

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:58.070
Maybe we should go to their 
apartment and check on them?

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.740
It seems they haven't returned 
to their apartment, either.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:04.400
Not even to their apartment?

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.980
Haven't returned...

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:08.850
Could that mean they never 
came back from the mountain?

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:11.920
We need to confirm that they're safe...

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.700
Mana's been all excited 
since they transferred in,

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:19.970
so I hadn't thought about it, 
but why did they come to our school?

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.930
It was a coincidence.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:28.030
School, huh?

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:33.600
We would have gone to school 
if we'd led a normal life.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.790
You're...

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.860
I knew it. You're the three Origami sisters.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.130
What?

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:41.610
How do you know us?

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.790
Nice to meet you.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:47.100
I'm the commander of Fifth Force, 
among other things.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.490
My name is Tierra.

00:03:48.490 --> 00:03:50.610
Fifth Force?!

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:51.660
Shh.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.160
Then you're their...

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.580
Hold on a second.

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.840
I've heard about you all.

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.210
About how you left Morgana, as well.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.930
S-So what about it?!

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:05.430
I've been worried about you.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.330
Worried?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.500
I'm sure you're having a difficult time.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:15.980
Anyone would be worried if they heard 
that three girls were suddenly

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:17.820
left alone in this world.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:19.860
What do you care?

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:24.100
You're trying to be nice just 
to capture us, aren't you?!

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.120
There are a lot of things I want to ask, but...

00:04:27.890 --> 00:04:31.050
I'm more worried about 
how you're living right now.

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:34.020
Could you leave that to me?

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:35.580
Leave it to you?

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:41.040
Yes. I can't just leave someone in trouble.

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:44.710
I'm a teacher at this school, after all.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:48.010
So that's what happened.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:51.660
They agreed to transfer in,

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.410
but they didn't want to live in the dorms.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.390
Why not?

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:58.150
The three of them, especially Akara-san,

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.110
didn't want to trouble others 
with taking care of them.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:06.490
I guess, as the eldest, she wants 
to provide for her sisters herself.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:11.580
Yeah, Akara-chan really cares 
about her younger sisters.

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:15.590
They didn't get stranded 
out in the snow, did they?

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:21.590
I see.

00:05:21.890 --> 00:05:26.090
So you've grown close to them too, huh?

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.930
How truly interesting.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:31.760
Especially that girl.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:38.320
It's a good chance to 
give you all one more job.

00:05:41.620 --> 00:05:43.860
Hina-chan was absent again today.

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:45.610
Koori-san, too.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:50.000
We checked almost every place we 
could think of in the neighborhood...

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:52.530
Maybe they went to another town far away.

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:56.180
Or maybe they returned 
to the fifth dimension.

00:05:56.180 --> 00:05:58.790
If only I'd been better friends to them...

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.140
This isn't your fault, Mana.

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:06.540
That's right. I'm sure they had a reason 
for disappearing all of a sudden.

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:08.590
A reason, huh...

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:11.680
You know, when we last fought...

00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:13.740
Akara-chin, stop it!

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.060
Remember when we all played 
together at the orphanage!

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:19.100
I don't want to remember that place.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.390
She said something like that.
Maybe that has something to do with it?

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.530
Mana-san, did something happen at the 
orphanage with Akara-san and the others?

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:32.490
Akara-chin was like the leader there.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:37.540
I don't think the three of them 
were bullied or harassed...

00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:43.960
So I'm still not sure why 
Akara-chin said that...

00:06:46.820 --> 00:06:48.510
Hina-san...

00:06:48.970 --> 00:06:51.890
I think I'm going to help you instead, Sacchan.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.190
What?

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:56.600
You have something you 
have to accomplish, right?

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:03.220
Eterno's Stella Prism has 
become unstable, moshu.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:04.730
Unstable?

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.710
What do you mean?

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:09.760
I've detected some strange interference, moshu.

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.240
Excuse me.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:14.520
What's wrong?

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:19.100
I think I should tell you about this...

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:19.660
Huh?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.710
About my memories.

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:27.840
You mean how your friends were taken out 
by Morgana in the world you were in?

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:33.300
No, it's possible that I didn't 
come from another world...

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.860
What's wrong?

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:38.100
You're...

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.310
<i>It's been a while, Odagiri-sensei.</i>

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.560
Do you know her?

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.740
She's the physics teacher that 
transferred here a month ago.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:49.990
Orie-sensei, why are you...

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.860
<i>I've finally found you.</i>

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:56.240
<i>I've been searching for you this whole time,</i>

00:07:56.920 --> 00:07:58.810
<i>Miyama Tsubame-san.</i>

00:07:58.810 --> 00:07:59.660
For me?

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:02.920
Searching for Tsubame-san?

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.880
<i>Yes. That's why I took this form.</i>

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:08.130
Morgana?!

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:14.050
Akara-san! Hina-san! Koori-san!

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:18.960
<i>Miyama Tsubame-san, if you come to me alone,</i>

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.020
<i>I'll return these three.</i>

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.920
<i>If you refuse my proposal,</i>

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:28.400
<i>these three will perish, 
so it's a little insurance.</i>

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:30.650
<i>I'll be waiting for you.</i>

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.740
This is...

00:08:33.310 --> 00:08:34.990
Five-dimensional coordinates, moshu!

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:38.490
So she took those girls...

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:42.200
Tierra-sensei, Moshune-chan!

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.390
It's gotta be a trap!

00:08:47.390 --> 00:08:48.170
It's dangerous!

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:49.800
Tsubame!

00:08:50.740 --> 00:08:55.130
You all became friends with 
me when I was a stranger.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.140
I can't call Akara-san and her 
sisters close friends yet,

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.950
but they're your friends, right?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:03.630
Yeah.

00:09:03.630 --> 00:09:05.230
Important friends!

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:08.690
So I have to save them.

00:09:12.600 --> 00:09:17.080
Before I came to this world, 
I had my run-ins with Morgana.

00:09:17.080 --> 00:09:19.780
I was fighting her along with everyone.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.070
What?

00:09:21.070 --> 00:09:22.680
With everyone?

00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:23.940
What do you mean?

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:26.770
Tsubame-san, have your memories returned?

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:27.500
What?

00:09:27.940 --> 00:09:29.880
I still don't know more than that.

00:09:30.290 --> 00:09:31.620
That's why I have to go.

00:09:31.620 --> 00:09:36.170
I need to find out where I came from,
and where I'm going from here.

00:09:36.820 --> 00:09:40.390
This is my problem.

00:09:41.230 --> 00:09:42.100
Tsubame.

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:43.680
Io?

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:46.140
Okay.

00:09:46.140 --> 00:09:47.690
But if it gets dangerous...

00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:51.000
We'll all come to save you!

00:09:52.900 --> 00:09:55.860
The other teams are standing by, too.

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:01.410
Moshune-chan, do it!

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:03.450
All ready, moshu.

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:35.650
Father, what should I do?

00:10:36.390 --> 00:10:41.600
I guess it's best to ask Fifth Force 
if they'd like assistance,

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.940
but I don't even have 
the courage to ask them.

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:47.080
Also, they have a Stella Prism.

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:49.920
<b>Collect all the Stella Prisms around the world 
that defy reason and destroy them. 
You have that power.</b>

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.920
It defies reason,

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:56.340
but they're protecting the 
world with their Stella Prisms.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:59.170
What should I believe?

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:02.210
With the personality I have,

00:11:02.210 --> 00:11:10.180
I put on that mask so that I can 
fight and steal when I need to...

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:13.550
Oh!

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.820
What's Tsubame-san's situation?

00:11:22.820 --> 00:11:25.270
The teleportation should be 
completed shortly, moshu.

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:26.280
Huh?

00:11:26.690 --> 00:11:27.790
I've lost her, moshu.

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.040
What?!

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.290
What do you mean?

00:11:30.620 --> 00:11:34.880
Tsubame-chan was teleported to a 
completely different dimension, moshu!

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.020
That can't be true...

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:40.310
Then Tsubame-chan will end 
up like the three sisters...

00:11:40.310 --> 00:11:42.090
Does that mean we can't find her?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:43.550
It can't be...

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:47.310
Who knew that Morgana could do that?

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:50.210
There's one thing I don't understand.

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:51.440
What is it, Satoka-chan?

00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:55.070
If Morgana is so powerful,

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:57.990
then couldn't she have just taken her by force?

00:11:58.530 --> 00:12:01.070
Why do something so elaborate?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:04.300
There might be some specific reason.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.180
Well, at any rate,

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:08.960
if we can't figure out where Morgana is...

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:12.210
We can't save Tsubame either, huh?

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.630
Moshune-chin, is there anything we can do?

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:18.750
Unfortunately not... I'm sorry, moshu.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:20.430
That can't be...

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:23.090
Wait, maybe Odile could...

00:12:23.460 --> 00:12:24.590
Odile?

00:12:27.350 --> 00:12:28.680
That voice...

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.030
It couldn't be...

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:32.140
It's been a while, everyone!

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:35.520
The Knight of the Black Swan, Odile, is here!

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:36.980
Odile!

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:43.780
Why are you here?

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:46.020
I... uh...

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:48.090
Well... Those guys...

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:51.200
The three Origami sisters. Them.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.250
You know them, right?

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:57.020
I, um, heard they haven't been around lately.

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:58.650
So I just kind of...

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.630
Just kind of was worried about them.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:04.980
A-And the middle sister kind 
of helped me out, and stuff.

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:08.090
Anyway, who cares about me?!

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:11.360
You have some information, right?

00:13:11.360 --> 00:13:13.850
Now just tell me.

00:13:14.980 --> 00:13:16.270
Thank you, Sacchin.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.400
What?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:19.730
That was good timing, Tanaka-san.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:20.770
What?

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:24.030
We were waiting for you, Tanaka Sachiko-san.

00:13:25.160 --> 00:13:27.010
H-Hold on a second!

00:13:27.010 --> 00:13:30.330
I-I'm the Knight of the Black Swan, Odile!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:35.040
I'm... I'm not a pure maiden 
like Tanaka Sachiko-san!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.800
Huh? Where are we?

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:54.720
Akara-chin!

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:57.440
Hina-chin! Koori-chin!

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:11.870
Welcome.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.740
Where are the three girls?!

00:14:14.110 --> 00:14:15.760
No need to worry.

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.870
I've returned them, as promised.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:22.240
I only need you.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:24.710
Tell me. Why me?!

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:28.680
You were the last one in Fifth Force.

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:30.050
Last one?

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:35.140
If I'd defeated you, humanity 
wouldn't have had any recourse,

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:36.930
and it would have perished.

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:39.600
According to my plan.

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:43.330
That's right.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:49.010
My precious friends were defeated, 
and I went to my last fight.

00:14:49.010 --> 00:14:51.780
And the next thing I knew, I was in this world.

00:14:52.180 --> 00:14:56.040
Then it's true. Those visions...

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:59.260
Those memories were of the future!

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:04.120
When you force yourself into the past,

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:07.380
the original you from that time also vanishes.

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:10.980
That's why you lost your memories.

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:15.290
That's right. This world was destroyed.

00:15:15.290 --> 00:15:16.500
For certain.

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:22.800
However, at that moment, 
you disappeared from the world.

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:26.190
You didn't die. You vanished.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:28.300
And that's when I formed a hypothesis,

00:15:28.300 --> 00:15:31.610
and then I searched for you to prove it.

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:33.320
Prove...

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:36.560
Yes, Miyama Tsubame-san...

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:41.040
The hypothesis that stated 
that you are Morgana.

00:15:41.880 --> 00:15:43.100
I see...

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:45.000
So we were taken by Morgana...

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.750
Sorry. I guess we caused you a lot of trouble.

00:15:48.260 --> 00:15:50.590
It's not your fault.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:51.470
But...

00:15:52.520 --> 00:15:55.600
In exchange for our lives, she...

00:15:56.230 --> 00:15:57.260
Yeah...

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:59.640
Akara-nee, Hina-nee.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:01.430
We have to save her.

00:16:01.430 --> 00:16:02.560
Yeah.

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.400
Yeah!

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:05.780
No, not just the three of you.

00:16:05.780 --> 00:16:06.310
What?!

00:16:06.990 --> 00:16:09.690
We're all going, right?

00:16:10.290 --> 00:16:11.650
All of us?

00:16:11.900 --> 00:16:13.490
We're all friends.

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:17.370
Yes, friends.

00:16:19.260 --> 00:16:20.660
Friends...

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:25.220
Oh, how I envy that sort of thing...

00:16:25.940 --> 00:16:27.320
Tanaka Sachiko-san.

00:16:27.320 --> 00:16:28.370
Y-Yes?

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:33.050
Wait, no! I told you, I'm Odile!

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:36.050
Odile, please help us.

00:16:36.310 --> 00:16:38.860
O-Of course.

00:16:38.860 --> 00:16:42.350
I'd be completely oblivious 
if I just left right now.

00:16:42.800 --> 00:16:45.370
We need your help.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:49.060
You're the daughter of the 
inventor of the Stella Prisms,

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:50.900
Professor Isami, are you not?

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:53.780
H-How do you...

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:56.740
It all happened twenty years ago.

00:16:57.130 --> 00:17:02.700
A small meteorite crashed down, 
and that was the start of everything.

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:07.540
There was an unknown particle, 
the Fifth particle, on the meteorite.

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:11.550
And the man who discovered it 
was her father, Professor Isami.

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:14.480
Through his research,

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:20.070
the professor discovered that the Fifth particle 
allowed travel between parallel worlds.

00:17:20.820 --> 00:17:25.510
And he developed the base technologies that 
led to the solidification of the particles,

00:17:25.510 --> 00:17:29.180
which allowed them to be controlled as 
Stella Prisms, as well as the memoca,

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:32.730
which store the quantum transformation 
of information from parallel worlds.

00:17:33.470 --> 00:17:36.930
And when the people who were 
showered with the Fifth particle

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:42.740
from the meteorite's landing had children, 
those children were affected.

00:17:42.740 --> 00:17:43.950
Children...

00:17:44.330 --> 00:17:49.420
Those children were born with a special ability.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:52.710
In short, the ability to detect parallel worlds.

00:17:52.710 --> 00:17:54.630
Are you talking about...

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.670
Us?

00:17:55.930 --> 00:18:01.160
Yes. And the orphanage that collected 
those children with no families

00:18:01.160 --> 00:18:04.680
was the one that Mana-san and the 
others were at, Jupiter Orphanage.

00:18:05.540 --> 00:18:07.390
That's the first time I've heard that!

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:08.870
I knew it...

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:12.620
I heard about that.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:17.030
So these are the girls...

00:18:18.040 --> 00:18:19.990
Experimentation stock.

00:18:20.230 --> 00:18:21.640
Experimentation?

00:18:31.970 --> 00:18:37.170
That was why I ran away with my sisters.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:38.830
But...

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:42.600
We weren't used for experimentation at all!

00:18:42.900 --> 00:18:44.930
The director was really nice, too.

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:46.930
Then the director...

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:49.730
My father wouldn't do something like that!

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:55.800
Yes, your father wanted you 
to use your special powers

00:18:55.800 --> 00:19:02.660
for the future through your own will.

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:04.090
The future...

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:06.120
Then what did we see?

00:19:06.760 --> 00:19:09.100
In contrast to that desire,

00:19:09.100 --> 00:19:12.540
some were attempting to make 
military use out of that research.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:16.190
They visited the professor often.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:17.760
I see...

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:22.640
The professor refused them, 
and then he went missing.

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:29.460
"Collect all the Stella Prisms around the world 
that defy reason and destroy them"...

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.870
So that's what you meant,

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:35.570
Father...

00:19:36.580 --> 00:19:37.860
Sacchan...

00:19:38.370 --> 00:19:39.990
After that, we...

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:49.250
<i>We're going to get 
experimented on and killed!</i>

00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.210
I can't run any further...

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:54.210
Koori!

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:01.090
I'm hungry...

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:04.490
Hina... Koori...

00:20:04.490 --> 00:20:05.830
Stay strong.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:11.600
I'm going to protect... both of you...

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:15.590
Who are you?

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.160
I'll save you.

00:20:20.640 --> 00:20:23.280
So who is Morgana, anyway?

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:25.780
One who has learned universal reason.

00:20:25.780 --> 00:20:27.240
She said that often.

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:31.890
So Eterno was built after the professor fled?

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:33.370
Yes.

00:20:33.600 --> 00:20:36.480
We continued our research 
on the Fifth particle

00:20:36.480 --> 00:20:39.460
and the Stella Prisms for purposes of peace

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.740
after the professor disappeared.

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:45.970
But during that time,

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:50.720
we detected a threat 
from a different dimension.

00:20:51.140 --> 00:20:53.060
And that was the O'bli?

00:20:53.060 --> 00:20:53.800
Yes.

00:20:54.480 --> 00:20:56.700
In order to oppose that threat,

00:20:56.700 --> 00:21:01.190
we hurried to train soldiers who had 
the special Fifth particle abilities.

00:21:02.160 --> 00:21:06.080
And that's when we created this 
place, Goryoukan Academy,

00:21:06.080 --> 00:21:09.320
with consultation from Jupiter Orphanage.

00:21:11.420 --> 00:21:15.160
The academy grounds were also 
where the meteorite fell, moshu.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.460
What?!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:18.380
You mean the meteorite fell here?

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.050
That's correct, moshu.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:22.980
You could say that we were able to 
build Eterno in the fifth dimension

00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:26.900
specifically because this place has so much 
relation to the Stella Prisms, moshu.

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:29.450
And you are the same...

00:21:29.450 --> 00:21:32.640
No, you have an even greater power.

00:21:32.640 --> 00:21:34.920
Y-Yeah.

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:38.440
So, what do you want me to do?

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:41.070
We want you to find Morgana's location.

00:21:41.070 --> 00:21:43.280
M-Morgana's location?

00:21:43.510 --> 00:21:46.990
You were going after Morgana's 
Stella Prism before, right?

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:51.990
I was able to detect it because I just happened 
to be on the same dimensional border.

00:21:51.990 --> 00:21:53.080
Please!

00:21:53.080 --> 00:21:55.230
We have to save Tsubame-chin!

00:21:55.230 --> 00:21:56.500
Please help us.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.460
I'd like to, but...

00:21:58.460 --> 00:22:02.500
If you have some sort of track to follow, 
there's hope, at least...

00:22:06.830 --> 00:22:09.330
The same smell as her...

00:22:09.330 --> 00:22:10.540
Smell?

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:13.550
Odile?!

00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:17.480
This is it!

00:22:25.700 --> 00:22:28.360
I'm... Morgana?

00:22:28.940 --> 00:22:33.760
The ability to change events that 
have passed through one's own will...

00:22:34.320 --> 00:22:38.920
Do you think a human with that ability exists?

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:41.640
When I...

00:22:41.640 --> 00:22:44.500
Back then... the world... my friends...

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:48.630
I saw it all get destroyed,

00:22:48.630 --> 00:22:50.680
and I wished from the bottom 
of my heart. That's all.

00:22:51.700 --> 00:22:54.140
I'm not the same as you!

00:22:54.400 --> 00:22:55.960
That's fine.

00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:58.330
If you want to insist on that,

00:22:58.330 --> 00:23:01.840
we can just replay everything 
again and verify it.

00:23:01.840 --> 00:23:02.860
Replay?

00:23:03.110 --> 00:23:06.910
I already tested that out 
on the snowy mountain.

00:23:06.910 --> 00:23:07.820
The snowy mountain?!

00:23:09.500 --> 00:23:10.570
You can't mean...

00:23:10.860 --> 00:23:12.060
Replay...

00:23:12.610 --> 00:23:16.960
In other words, here in this world, this age...

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:24.980
I can reproduce exactly what 
I had happen back then.

00:23:35.970 --> 00:23:40.980
<b>Final Battle! Fifth Force Forever</b>

00:23:37.300 --> 00:23:40.980
"Final Battle! Fifth Force Forever!"
